y is it significantly harder  but he essentially becomes  indestructible at least for about a  minute this means that he can nullify  virtually any attack that's thrown at  him  in fact I reckon he could probably  withstand a punch or two from this guy  and we saw this demonstrated in the show  when that villain was easily pissing his  skin before he used unbreakable butt and  once he turned on unbreakable suddenly  that villain couldn't even touch him and  whilst he can't hold it for too long  right now remember that Kirishima is  still a first-year students so so by the  time he graduates I reckon he could  probably have it up to about 10 minute  so more and unlike his usual form this  unbreakable mode should not wear off  based on the number of hits he's taken  at least that's what we thought those of  you who have read even further in the  manga will know that this form was  pretty effortlessly destroyed by rapper  in one of the best fights of the overall  arc and for me this kind of took away  the amazement as seeing unbreakable for  the first time because it kind of hurts  to see it be destroyed so easily but to  kill regime is credit he did still put  up one hell of a fight by continuously  reharden himself after getting worn down  but the fact remains that unbreakable  was still beaten down by rapper and  let's be real here rapper is a strong  villain but he is by far by far is not  nowhere close to being the strongest  villain we've seen in my ear academia so  if he can do that imagine what an actual  boss villain could do and then we have  to move on to the joint training art  with class one be your Ashima in this  arc was again taken out quite quickly  despite being in unbreakable mode this  guy from class 1b whose name I don't  actually know basically just picture  Shima and threw him up in the air and I  know the quirk is called unbreakable not  on throwable but still the fact that he  can just pick up Kirishima and not start  bleeding because remember 